From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:11:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: write every channel of a swizzled colour
 attachment

Metal refuses a swizzled view of a renderable texture, so a colour format
whose channels Metal only offers in another order, such as
VK_FORMAT_B4G4R4A4_UNORM_PACK16 on A4B4G4R4, is rendered to in the
hardware's order with the shader moving the channels. The lowering
reordered the stored value and left the store's width alone, but a store
names the attachment channels it writes as its own leading lanes: a
fragment shader that writes fewer than four channels then wrote the
hardware's leading lanes instead of the lanes those channels live in, so
the last channel it wrote was never stored and the lane it did write held
a component the value does not have. An OpenGL ES 3.2 guest saw it as
dEQP-GLES3.functional.fragment_out.{basic,array}.fixed.rgba4_* failing
for the float, vec2 and vec3 outputs and passing for vec4: the channel
after the ones that happened to line up came back undefined.

Rebuild such a store over all four lanes in the hardware's order and let
its write mask name the lanes the shader actually wrote, and read a load
back the same way. Move the pass into its own file so a test can reach
it, and cover every channel count and both channel orders.
